1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
The Clover Kingdom.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In this place where magic is everything,

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
there lives one boy who was born without it.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
His name is Asta.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
His strength and determination helped him become a magic knight.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
And despite the many challenges he faces,

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
he aims for the top and refuses to give up.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Rich or poor, royalty or commoner,

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Asta believes anyone can shine.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
His mission is to prove that to the whole world

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
and to become the next Wizard King.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The Clover Kingdom.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The Clover Kingdom.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Dad Rick Re sees another some song about Aaron Smith.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The Clover Kingdom.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
The Clover Kingdom.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:42,980
I'll see you next time.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:02:12,980
I'll see you next time.

19
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:43,000


20
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,380
But he controls Salamander now, too.

21
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,880
And there's Lord Nozel.

22
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,860
His bangs are dreamy.

23
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,560
I heard that he was on the front lines during that last battle.

24
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,200
Lady Charlotte!

25
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:59,080
I don't see Yami or the green praying mantis, Captain.

26
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:02,920
How dare they be late on an important occasion such as this?

27
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:04,840
There's Rell!

28
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,840
Uh, is he okay?

29
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,840
Looks like he's spacing out there.

30
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:09,680
Oh, yeah.

31
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:10,680
I know that face.

32
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,360
He's definitely in love.

33
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:14,480
That wonderful girl.

34
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,900
I wonder where she is now.

35
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:20,100
Mr. Rill's first love.

36
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,260
Great news, madam.

37
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,340
Your precious little boy is starting to become a man.

38
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:28,020
I'd say it's only a matter of time before you'll be a grandmother.

39
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:29,440
Wow, look.

40
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,600
It's Lady Dorothy.

41
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:31,780
He's awake.

42
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,900
Who knew she had such pretty eyes?

43
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:34,980
Hey there.

44
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,000
How is everybody?

45
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,640
Lord Kaiser looks awfully dapper today.

46
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,060
Yeah, but he seems a little down.

47
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:41,740
Huh.

48
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:43,600
Check it out.

49
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,120
The man of the hour!

50
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,400
Wizard King!

51
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:53,660
Oh no, is he injured?

52
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,260
I guess so.

53
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,100
I heard he was the one who stopped the eye of the midnight sun back when they attacked the

54
00:03:59,100 --> 00:03:59,800
royal capital.

55
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:04,000
Goodness, he must have been through such a terrible ordeal to protect all of us.

56
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,220
I hope he isn't in too much pain.

57
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,880
We'll never forget what he did.

58
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,140
Go Wizard King!

59
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,460
What?

60
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:14,200
You want me to pose as you?

61
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,560
That's ridiculous!

62
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:20,220
Perhaps, but I can't exactly go marching into the capital looking like a child.

63
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:22,660
There'd be trouble if the king saw me this way.

64
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,600
And of course, not appearing at all would be suspicious.

65
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,700
True, but don't you think they'll know the difference?

66
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:31,860
I've already thought through the whole thing.

67
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,200
All you have to do is stand up there and wave.

68
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,780
Here, cover your face with these.

69
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:37,240
What?

70
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,220
Your appearance is different now, but inside you're the same as you ever were.

71
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:43,080
Just smile and wave and pray they don't notice.

72
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,360
We're sorry.

73
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:53,460
The Wizard King has a sore throat today, so sadly he won't be able to speak to you all.

74
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,900
Please excuse him.

75
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:57,940
Oh, I was looking forward to hearing from him.

76
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,120
Well, these things happen.

77
00:04:59,280 --> 00:04:59,600
Yeah.

78
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:05,700
Now, I'd like everyone to give a round of applause to the valiant hero who stood up to our enemies

79
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:12,660
and protected our beloved kingdom, our illustrious ruler, Augustus Kiriclover XIII.

80
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,580
Oh, hey, he's here, too.

81
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:17,400
He's okay, I guess.

82
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,320
Thanks for your help.

83
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,840
Why are you dawdling back there?

84
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:24,460
Pick up the pace, knave!

85
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,120
This is my one moment of glory, you know!

86
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,000
Sahari!

87
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,800
Oh, how the heck did I end up being errand boy to this king?

88
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:34,340
It turns out going with the flow is for chunks.

89
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:37,060
How dare you stand in my royal bubble!

90
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,300
Same goes for you!

91
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,060
Curse you, Julius.

92
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:47,300
Now I'm responsible for addressing the people, all because you have a little tickle in your pathetic throat!

93
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:54,000
Then again, this might be the perfect opportunity to demonstrate my superior dignity and benevolence!

94
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,420
You poor fool!

95
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:58,240
I hope you enjoyed the attention while it lasted!

96
00:05:59,380 --> 00:05:59,860
Ahem!

97
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:03,400
Greetings and salutations to all my loyal subjects!

98
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:07,480
Your king, Augustus Kiriclover XIII, is gracing you with his presence!

99
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,720
What's this?

100
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,480
They're at a loss for words!

101
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:14,420
They must be stunned by my immaculate visage!

102
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,820
Is he almost done, or...?

103
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:17,440
Shhh...

104
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:17,780
Yes.

105
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:22,020
As you can see, the public awaits your kingly wisdom with bated breath, Majesty.

106
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:26,000
But please make it as brief as possible, lest the suspense kill them.

107
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,280
Uh, of course!

108
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:29,820
I beg your pardon!

109
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,040
The king takes orders from no one!

110
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:33,360
Ahem!

111
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:37,580
Thanks to my brave deeds with minimal assistance from the magic knights,

112
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,000
the Eye of the Midnight Sun has fled,

113
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,900
and peace has finally been restored to the Clover Kingdom!

114
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:43,920
You're so welcome!

115
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:49,120
None of this would have been possible without the impressive things I do on a daily basis!

116
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:52,000
However, I imagine some of you are still concerned.

117
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,020
How will your lives change?

118
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:57,060
What if another enemy tries to attack us?

119
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,300
But I promise there's no need for that!

120
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:00,780
Hawk!

121
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,180
Witness my splendid light magic!

122
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,400
How majestic!

123
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,560
How striking!

124
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,060
Light magic!

125
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,860
Absolute monarch of divine brilliance!

126
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:12,280
Perfection!

127
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,860
And so, my adoring public!

128
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:19,500
As long as the Clover Kingdom remains in my capable hands,

129
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,500
it shall always be safe!

130
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,180
Lay all your cares and doubts upon my shoulders!

131
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:32,000
Damn it!

132
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,380
That's enough, Beanpole!

133
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,560
Let's settle this feud once and for all!

134
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,320
Care, care!

135
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,120
You don't have to ask me twice!

136
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,840
Time to put your money where your mouth is, foreigner!

137
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,240
Hey, wait!

138
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,000
What's going on?

139
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:45,440
What is this, a party?

140
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,180
Yami, Jack...

141
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:49,400
I know, I told you to.

142
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,040
We had an important event planned today.

143
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:56,440
We were supposed to gather in the square and tell everyone that the enemy's been defeated.

144
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:57,860
Oh, was that today?

145
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:58,900
Care, care!

146
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,280
Must have slipped my mind.

147
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:04,240
Picking unnecessary fights is not an acceptable reason to show up late!

148
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,460
Trust me, he's the one who started it.

149
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,320
That's a lie!

150
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,780
We were both there, you know damn well what happened.

151
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,280
I think we've heard enough from the two of you.

152
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:14,340
This is hardly the time or place.

153
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:15,360
Tch!

154
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:19,420
Goodness, both of those squads are so violent!

155
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:21,560
You saw the paper, right?

156
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,920
They say one of the black bulls is possessed by a devil.

157
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,920
That makes sense.

158
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:29,720
When they placed second at the Star Festival, I knew they must have had outside help.

159
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:30,780
Exactly.

160
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,320
Everyone knows they're the worst squad.

161
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:35,060
Why, you irreverent ingrates!

162
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:38,760
How dare you intrude upon my invincible light magic spell!

163
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:39,300
Huh?

164
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:40,560
Your what?

165
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,040
Don't test me!

166
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:44,360
You brute stepped right into my spotlight!

167
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:49,000
Your highness, perhaps this is a chance to show the people your leniency.

168
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:52,380
If they see how merciful you are, they'll like you more.

169
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:53,680
Oh, is that so?

170
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,560
Who wants your opinion?

171
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:58,840
Just because you've been hailed as a hero, give me a break!

172
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:03,000
I mean, I must applaud your fervor.

173
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:05,940
By all means, gentlemen, keep being your raucous selves.

174
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:08,820
It's a symbol of your passion for our great land.

175
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:09,580
Sure.

176
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,520
And now his majesty will take his leave.

177
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,680
Let's give him one more round of applause.

178
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:18,460
Um, excuse me, Captain Jack.

179
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:22,860
Look, anytime you want me to come back to the praying mantises, just give me a holler.

180
00:09:23,060 --> 00:09:23,820
Come back?

181
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,420
Who the hell are you?

182
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,820
Attention to me, servant boy!

183
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,460
Uh, be right there.

184
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,600
Is he one of your guys?

185
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:35,380
You really think I let a wuss like that on my squad?

186
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:40,220
I suppose it's about time for us to head out as well.

187
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:41,280
Yeah, I guess.

188
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,220
Okay, later!

189
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,400
Lord Vondance!

190
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,680
Thank goodness it's over.

191
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,320
You gonna explain your outfit, Doc?

192
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,980
Or do we have to guess?

193
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:52,740
What?

194
00:09:52,740 --> 00:10:10,820
Yikes!

195
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,580
All of the Magic Knight captains in the same room!

196
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:16,220
Kind of hard not to feel like we're under a lot of pressure.

197
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:19,100
Yeah, if this is supposed to be a meeting for captains,

198
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,540
then I wonder why they wanted all of us to be a part of it.

199
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:24,980
I should apologize, Yami.

200
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,920
You and the Black Bulls are the ones who deserve that praise.

201
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,480
And yet the audience mostly cheered for me.

202
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:33,100
We're kind of used to getting booed, actually.

203
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,720
Right, I'm sorry.

204
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,140
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

205
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,780
Just forget about it.

206
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,080
Calm down.

207
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,940
Don't let your heart go aflutter.

208
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:43,000
Just relax and breathe.

209
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,740
What's wrong, prickly princess?

210
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:47,660
Your face is all red.

211
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:48,720
Feeling okay?

212
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,260
I'm perfectly all right!

213
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:52,660
Listen...

214
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:56,360
If you need to take a dump, it's not healthy to hold it in.

215
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:56,900
Just go.

216
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:58,780
That's not the issue at all!

217
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,400
How can a person be so utterly devoid of tact?

218
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,580
So I was wrong?

219
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:03,680
Dead wrong!

220
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,060
You really don't get it, do you, Yami?

221
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:09,200
No wonder everyone's calling you a clueless idiot.

222
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,200
He needs to piss!

223
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,120
He needs to piss!

224
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,000
No!

225
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,720
And they're in charge.

226
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,820
Are they like that all the time?

227
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,060
I wish this was shocking to me.

228
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:26,100
Forcing us to come to a meeting and then being the last person to show up, if that's not typical Julius, I don't know what is.

229
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,720
I bet you anything he forgot about all this.

230
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:32,040
He's probably off goofing around somewhere like a little idiot.

231
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,520
Crazy old man.

232
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,540
A crazy old kid, I guess.

233
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,600
I hate to say it, but you're right.

234
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,040
Shameful.

235
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,580
Yeah, that's true.

236
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:41,820
He's so silly.

237
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:42,940
Agreed.

238
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,920
Any idea what his problem is?

239
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:47,640
Nope.

240
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,740
He's been stuck like that since the curse broke, apparently.

241
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:55,220
I'm sorry for the wait, everyone.

242
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,080
Excellent.

243
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,800
I see you all made it.

244
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:00,960
Him again?

245
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:02,480
The Matio.

246
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,560
They asked him to come too?

247
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,000
Pardon the delay.

248
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,600
Careful.

249
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:12,300
If you try to condemn one of my squad members again, I swear I will...

250
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:16,180
Yami, I'm the one who summoned him here, so there's no need to fight.

251
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:17,540
Wait, you were invited?

252
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,500
So it would seem.

253
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,140
Apparently, the topic in question involves me.

254
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,920
I was informed that my presence was required.

255
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,100
Our meeting today is about the devil residing in the Spade Kingdom.

256
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:35,500
Recently, some of our magic knights paid a visit to the Heart Kingdom,

257
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,760
hoping to gather information about the devils.

258
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:41,460
I trust everyone's seen the reports by now.

259
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:45,820
However, since you all were there, we would like to hear it from you.

260
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:47,420
Please proceed.

261
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,360
Okay.

262
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,960
We'll do our best, sir.

263
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:56,900
In the Heart Kingdom, the strength of a mage is normally determined by a system called magic stages.

264
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:00,880
The ranking starts at nine, then eight, seven, and so on.

265
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:04,040
And the smaller the number, the stronger the mage.

266
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:09,680
According to Queen Laura Pechka, it's extremely rare and favorable to have mages at stage zero.

267
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:14,860
So whenever there's a battle, the side with the most warriors at that level is considered the superior one.

268
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:17,620
